  "Id": 129,
  "Title": "\u200b\u200bFostering effective early childhood education in Balochistan",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Early Childhood Development Project-Balochistan",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass3320A855CA77431C877F7E6EEE8C075E\"><p>\u200b</p><div>The <a href=\"/iedpk/pdc-karachi/Pages/home.aspx\">Professional Development Centre, Karachi</a> offered two <a href=\"/iedpk/cpe/Pages/home.aspx\">Continuing Professional Education (CPE) \u200b</a>programmes for early childhood educators and practitioners, under the Early Childhood Development Project-Balochistan funded by the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, Australia.</div><div><br></div><div>30 participants including government officials, faculty from different institutions and master trainers from Balochistan attended the programme titled, \u2018Introduction to Early Childhood Education Curriculum\u2019 conducted in Karachi from February 23 to March 6, 2015. The programme provided the participants an opportunity to enhance their understanding of the National Curriculum for Early Childhood Education (2007) and effective implementation of pedagogical strategies in the early years setting.</div><div><br></div><div>Another CPE programme titled \u2018Formative Classroom Assessment\u2019, which was conducted in Quetta from March 16-28, 2015, brought together 47 teachers and teacher educators from different institutes in Balochistan. The programme focused on enhancing the course participants\u2019 understanding of formative and summative assessment; the basic principles and methods of classroom assessment; and designing basic assessment tools for their own classrooms.</div><div><br></div><div>The participants\u2019 from both programmes appreciated the content knowledge and expertise of the faculty and the practical relevance, which the course had for the enhancement of their current job skills.</div></div>",
